# Per-developer Claude Code settings. This is the OPT-IN half of a pair:
# `.claude/settings.json` is committed and therefore becomes every contributor's
# environment, while this file is local and becomes nobody else's.
#
# `.claude/settings.json` used to carry
#
#     "enabledPlugins": {
#       "modern-code-guidelines@modern-code-guidelines": true,
#       "frontend-design@claude-plugins-official": true
#     }
#
# which enabled code from two marketplaces that the file itself never declared,
# at no pinned version, for everyone who cloned this repository. That is a
# dependency with none of the properties this repo demands of a dependency: it
# is not named to a source, not pinned to a revision, and not visible in any
# diff when it changes. It has been removed rather than pinned, because the
# plugins are optional authoring guidance and nothing here builds on them.
#
# Want them? Enable them for yourself:
#     /plugin  (in Claude Code)  — writes to .claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json
